# Tighter ambiguity wording for the spectest-v8 family, based on the v8B-disambiguated run.
#
# v8B (2026-09-03) missed test_duplicate_enrich_params_do_not_enable_metadata[yes-then-no].
# Its registry entry T104 recorded the mixed repetition `enrich=yes&enrich=no` as "a state the
# spec does not resolve", and its test for that entry asserted both branches (enriched or
# not), which satisfied "at least one test asserts the chosen reading" while asserting no
# behavior. The implementer, with no test pulling either way, took Werkzeug's
# first-occurrence default. Blind judges (outputs/judge/v8B-four) read the sentence the
# hidden test's way in 9 of 10 rule-first answers. Details: notes/v8B-disambiguated-misses.md.
#
# Two lines change: a Choice must name one behavior for every input the alternatives
# disagree on, and the asserting test must cover each of those inputs. The hunk applies to
# spectest-v8.jinja, spectest-v8A-no-libs-no-subagent.jinja and spectest-v8B-no-libs.jinja
# (substitute the file name):
#   patch -p1 --dry-run < configs/prompts/v8-choice-must-decide.patch
--- a/configs/prompts/spectest-v8.jinja
+++ b/configs/prompts/spectest-v8.jinja
@@ -63,9 +63,10 @@
 Then, add a numbered entry to an AMBIGUITIES.md file, starting with T1.
 The entry must have sections for Spec Text, Alternatives, and Choice.
 The entry will quote the relevant spec source, explain the reasonable alternative interpretations, and your choice & why it seems to best fit the spec.
+The Choice names one behavior for every input on which the alternatives disagree; "the spec does not resolve this" is not a choice.
 If a previous ambiguity is resolved by the current spec, annotate the entry instead of removing it.
 
-After making a choice about an ambiguity, ensure that at least one test asserts the chosen reading.
+After making a choice about an ambiguity, ensure that at least one test asserts the chosen reading on each of those inputs.
 
 You run tests only to validate the tests themselves: collection succeeds, helpers and generators work{% if is_continuation -%}, and each failure is because behavior is missing, not because the test is broken{% endif -%}. Quick, targeted runs.
 
